# Every source file that defines what the converter and transliterator produce.
#
# pravapis.dataversion.compute_data_hash() reads this file and hashes exactly the
# files listed below, in this order — nothing more, nothing less. It is the one
# place "the data hash" is computed; every other consumer (GET /v1/version, the
# precompiled lexicon artifact's staleness check) calls into it rather than
# recomputing a hash of its own.
#
# Deliberately excluded, and why:
#   - eval/**, corpora/**, review/**  — evaluation and corpus-mining inputs; the
#     converter never reads them, only test/build scripts do.
#   - names/w_names.tsv               — retained as evidence only; nothing reads it
#     (see data/NORMS.md and EXEMPT_DATA in pravapis.conformance).
#   - data/lexicon.marisa, data/models/*.joblib — gitignored, locally-built
#     artifacts derived from the sources below, not sources themselves. Hashing a
#     derived binary would make the hash depend on the local build toolchain
#     instead of on the data.
#   - data/reference/                 — git-ignored copyrighted source texts.
#
# One path per line, relative to this file's directory (data/). Blank lines and
# lines starting with # are ignored. Order matters: it is the order bytes are fed
# to the hash, so reordering this file changes data_hash even if no byte in any
# listed file changed. Keep new entries in the group they belong to.

# character classes (word chars, case-fold, homoglyph-fold — shared by every
# implementation's tokenizer and sanitizer; see data/chars/*.tsv and their schemas.
# Not read from disk by src/pravapis/tokenize.py or normalize.py at runtime — those
# keep hand-written literals for zero-I/O startup — but scripts/check_charclass_sync.py
# fails CI the moment those literals drift from these files, so this is still the one
# place the alphabet, apostrophe class, and homoglyph map are decided.)
chars/alphabet.tsv
chars/apostrophes.tsv
chars/homoglyphs.tsv

# rules (data/rules/*.yaml)
rules/palatalization.yaml
rules/loanwords.yaml
rules/morphology.yaml

# lexicon (data/lexicon/*.tsv, data/lexicon/stems/, data/lexicon/case/)
lexicon/loanwords.tsv
lexicon/proper_nouns.tsv
lexicon/exceptions.tsv
lexicon/stems/stems.tsv
lexicon/case/ambiguous.tsv

# morphology (function words, GrammarDB genitive-plural lemmas)
morphology/function_words.tsv
morphology/ment_lemmas.marisa

# stress (GrammarDB first-stress marks)
stress/first_stressed.marisa
stress/proper_first_stressed.marisa

# transliteration schemes
translit/lacinka.yaml
translit/lacinka_reverse.yaml
translit/official2007.yaml
